config MESHTASTIC_HEAP_TRACE
	bool "Trace every _system_heap alloc/free to the log (diagnostic)"
	default n
	select SYS_HEAP_LISTENER
	help
	  Registers a Zephyr heap_listener on _system_heap (the general k_malloc
	  pool sized by CONFIG_HEAP_MEM_POOL_SIZE) and logs every allocation and
	  free with its size, pointer, and a running total maintained locally in
	  the listener (not by re-querying the heap, which would deadlock: the
	  listener callback runs with the heap's own spinlock held).

	  Built to answer a specific question: the periodic heap heartbeat
	  (meshtastic_watchdog.c) showed a flat steady-state allocated total but
	  a max_allocated (peak-since-boot) that drifted by a couple of KB
	  between boot sessions on the same board/build, with no per-event
	  visibility into what caused it. This turns that "peak observed
	  eventually" signal into an event-by-event timeline: what allocated,
	  how big, and when, correlated against boot time via the existing
	  network log timestamps.

	  Diagnostic only -- off by default. Adds one heap_listener struct pair
	  (~80 B) and a LOG_INF call on every heap event; leave off for normal
	  operation once the question above is answered, since a busy heap
	  (frequent MQTT reconnects, PhoneAPI churn) could log a lot.
